WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.743
Okay

00:00:00.743 --> 00:00:02.601
Steve, long time no see

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:08.620
Same to you, can I call you Yanchan? Don't know whether you are Chinese or Japanese?

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:12.630
Haha, just call me Yanchan. Yeah, I'm Chinese.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:16.590
What we are going to talk about today is that

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:25.780
even though the Chinese and the Japanese are different culturally and geographically, is it easy for them to learn each other's language

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.660
Yeah, that's the topic.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.260
I think it's very interesting

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:36.260
I'm interested because we're neither Chinese nor Japanese

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:40.390
We have certain problems when learning those languages

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:47.230
So the topic is, how easy it is for the Japanese and the Chinese to learn each other's language

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:53.080
But first, can you please do a self introduction please?

00:00:54.700 --> 00:01:00.340
Oh yeah, no problem. My name is Yang Xiaoxi and I come from Sichuan, China

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:08.020
I lived in Sichuan until I was 18 years old and majored in Japanese for my university in China

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:16.010
Then I came to Japan for studying at my third year of university, now I have been living in Japan for ten years

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:23.520
So I've been in Japan for a long time and I've spent about 1/3 of my life in Japan now

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:27.319
I have no problem communicating in Japanese, and that's my level of the language now

00:01:27.969 --> 00:01:28.991
Interesting

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:30.530
But my mother tongue is still Chinese

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:36.070
Now in Japan, how much is everyone interested in learning Chinese

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.910
what is the interest level

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:45.390
Well, I remember when I first came to Japan ten years ago

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:52.500
Almost no one can speak Chinese or very few Japanese are interested in China or Chinese

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:58.880
But after spending years in Japan especially since about two or three years ago

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:02.810
I noticed that many Japanese people around me began to learn Chinese

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:11.210
Whether they are employees learning for work or students choosing Chinese as their second language in college

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:17.060
Recently even many Japanese celebrities, singers, actors and entertainers are learning Chinese.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:26.740
I really feel that there are a lot of Japanese people learning Chinese now

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:38.310
Yep, that's how it feels like to me now.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.080
Okay, so can you say that now in Japan, Chinese has become a second language?

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:51.660
that is in addition to English, Chinese is the second language that people are willing to learn

00:02:52.330 --> 00:03:00.410
Sorry, it's a little hard to hear right now, maybe the network isn't working well, can you repeat?

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:05.770
Oh, okay. Can you hear well now?

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:12.560
Ah, now it's good. It stopped suddenly just now.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:19.520
Well, in Japan, English is the main foreign language

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:25.850
when people learn a foreign language, they learn English

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:32.380
Right

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:37.420
and the book store is full of English learning material for TOEFL

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:42.910
now that they have more interests in Chinese

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:52.470
Does it mean that Chinese is now the second most popular foreign language in Japan?

00:03:55.070 --> 00:04:00.950
Well, I think Chinese is probably the second most popular foreign language after English these days

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:08.040
but about 5 or 6 years ago, Korean was the second most popular foreign language

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:13.510
Because Korean seems to be easier for Japanese to learn in terms of similar grammar

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:16.210
So more Japanese people learn Korean in the past

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:19.200
Also Korean TV series and

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:26.750
Korean celebrities are very popular in Japan, so more Japanese people chose to learn Korean

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:36.530
but now Chinese is more likely to be used so there's a lot more Japanese people choosing Chinese than before so what's the main winter for people who are learning Chinese

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:38.200
so what's their main motivation of learning Chinese?

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:47.980
Well, it depends. Since I've been teaching Japanese Chinese since I was a college student

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:54.810
their reasons of learning Chinese vary

00:04:55.470 --> 00:05:03.910
for example, a student would think that learning Chinese may be useful in a career sense

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:12.250
Of course, English is a compulsory subject, but learning Chinese can also be useful for finding a job

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:16.290
And then there are the Japanese who are already working,

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:23.980
their companies have business associations with those in China, in which case,

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:30.410
they have to be able to speak Chinese a little bit for the job

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:39.610
and then there are housewives who love Chinese TV dramas and Chinese celebrities, so they began to learn Chinese

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:44.090
So there are cultural reasons as well

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:49.180
It's not just about career and

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:57.340
making money, some people learn because they are interested about

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:01.100
the modern and ancient culture of China

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:01.860
correct?

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:12.280
Yes, it's really interesting because these days, you know, a lot of Japanese celebrities are trying very hard to learn Chinese

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:16.270
and their fans would want to learn Chinese as well because of their idols

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:21.100
A lot of people actually learn Chinese because of this

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:28.830
Is it the same as the Korean BTS?

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:30.280
The famous....

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:35.620
Yeah yeah

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:45.170
I don't know anything about the BTS, I just know it's very popular all over the world

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:49.500
And they also speak English, Chinese and Thai

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:55.660
I like their spirit of learning foreign languages

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:02.670
So for learning Chinese, the Japanese

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:08.820
for sure has a lot of advantages over us, that is, people from European and American countries

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:17.180
they know most Chinese characters

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:24.770
but do you think Chinese is easier to learn for the Japanese?

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:32.150
as a Chinese who has learned Japanese, and now teaching the Japanese Chinese

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:41.830
I would think that Chinese should be easy Japanese to learn, because first of all, like what you just said

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:50.150
there are 2,000 Chinese characters regularly used in Japanese and we have a saying in Chinese

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:53.660
that is if you know 3000 Chinese characters, you can read any book or newspaper

00:07:54.370 --> 00:08:01.770
so basically you can understand the content of all books and newspapers with 3000 Chinese characters

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:10.950
and now the Japanese people already know 2000 characters, so it's about 70 percent of that

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:12.330
they should be able to understand more

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:19.460
so they should be able to read the characters very fast

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:24.450
But one interesting thing that I've noticed recently

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:33.840
I think perhaps it's easier for Chinese to learn Japanese than the Japanese to learn Chinese in terms of characters

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:35.360
Why?

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:39.890
Because an ordinary person from China, such as me from Sichuan

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:49.780
Although I've only learned simplified Chinese since childhood, but I can read all traditional Chinese characters

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:55.710
You know that there are simplified and traditional Chinese

00:08:56.110 --> 00:09:00.910
and Japanese has more traditional Chinese characters than simplified ones

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:07.780
but normally Chinese people know both,  but recently when I was teaching the Japanese Chinese

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:11.490
I found out that a lot of Japanese have never seen simplified characters before. so it was difficult for them to

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:20.080
match the simplified Chinese characters with the traditional ones, which means they can't read simplified Chinese

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:26.890
So regarding this, I think for the Japanese

00:09:27.990 --> 00:09:34.870
Chinese characters are a little bit unfamiliar and difficult to understand in the beginning

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:44.830
In addition to Chinese characters, it may be difficult for Japanese people to pronounce Chinese

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:50.750
Because you know that Chinese has four tones and even some

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:56.110
pronunciations that are not found in Japanese such as retro-flex and back nasal sound

00:09:56.780 --> 00:10:01.580
these pronunciations may be a little difficult for Japanese people in the beginning

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:10.210
But in terms of grammar I think Chinese is relatively simple, it's my personal opinion

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:16.590
Yeah, I agree.

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:23.900
Because when I started learning Chinese, I started with traditional Chinese for a few months

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:31.680
and then simplified Chinese, it was actually not a problem

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:41.190
because learning a foreign language is not a matter of weeks, not months, it takes a lot of time

00:10:41.710 --> 00:10:48.470
So at the beginning, the Japanese may not be able to read some Chinese characters

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:51.910
it's not a big problem because

00:10:52.540 --> 00:11:00.020
they might lack a little bit of something, but I don't think that's a big problem

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:05.530
I think pronunciation is a problem, and for us westerners

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:10.440
The biggest problem is the four tones and characters

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:16.300
the Japanese basically don't have a problem with the characters

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:19.820
But learning the four tones is an issue

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:27.110
This pronunciation can be a problem and I think except for the four tones

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:33.480
the pronunciation of Mandarin is close to that of English, the vowels

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:40.140
Ah yeah, right

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:48.360
so in that case, it's easier for the Japanese to learn Spanish and they might have some problems with the pronunciation of Chinese

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:52.600
But it's also a matter of habit, not a big problem

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:56.830
Yeah, but I also think that the pronunciation of Chinese

00:11:57.670 --> 00:12:05.750
whether or not you pronounce it right, it won't normally affect your understanding of the entire sentence

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:13.560
unless it's just one word

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:21.840
So I always think that in order to learn the four tones

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:29.480
don't just memorize it

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:33.790
you need to get used to how they are being used in a sentence

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.700
Practice with words

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:45.230
master the intonation, otherwise you won't be able to remember

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:50.840
but I I think that learning any language is just about your attitude

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:55.740
when a Japanese person learns Chinese

00:12:56.530 --> 00:13:04.570
they need to think of themselves as Chinese

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:07.540
to imitate

00:13:08.530 --> 00:13:11.770
Be willing to integrate in anther culture

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:20.540
that is the most important thing I think, of course you have to like it first

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:27.450
be interested and like to think of yourself as one of them

00:13:28.060 --> 00:13:35.660
with this attitude, your pronunciation will get better over time

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:46.310
Exactly. As you said before, whether a language is difficult or not

00:13:46.790 --> 00:13:50.590
has a lot to do with the language learner's native language

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:57.630
So I think whether it's Chinese learning Japanese or  Japanese learning Chinese

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:01.520
since the two cultures are so close

00:14:01.990 --> 00:14:04.390
There are many Chinese characters that are very similar

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:09.730
I don't think it's too difficult for either side to speak each other's language

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:14.490
I really still think English is more difficult than Japanese

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:19.960
I've started learning English since childhood but I am still not good at it

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:21.970
But the thing is

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:30.500
For example, if you're a Spanish speaker, it would be easy for you to learn Portuguese because the vocabulary would be pretty much the same

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:35.480
same with grammar, but that's also why it's not easy

00:14:36.130 --> 00:14:38.210
Because it's hard to leave

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:46.260
the Spanish environment to be a Portuguese

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:53.960
but it's fine with Turkey, Japanese or whatever

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:58.130
I think there might be situations when a Japanese

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:04.490
looks at a Chinese character but pronounces it in the Japanese way

00:15:05.490 --> 00:15:11.490
Maybe, but I'm not sure

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:20.110
yeah, Chinese and Japanese have some characters that are the same but with totally different meanings

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:22.270
yeah but not many

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:27.160
but it's a lot for beginners

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:35.710
and they often get confused, there are some interesting words

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:38.220
for example, (Japanese words)

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:52.490
(Japanese words) is when you are asked to do something that you don't really want to do

00:15:53.310 --> 00:16:02.950
what do you think is the biggest problem for Chinese to learn Japanese?

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:10.090
I think it's the grammar

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:14.750
it's what I can't get used to the most

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:19.430
Because in Chinese and English, we have subject, predicate, and then object

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:27.230
but in Japanese it's completely the other way around

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:33.040
they put the result at the end, yes or no comes out last

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:39.640
So I found it really hard to speak at first because it's very difficult for you to speak naturally and fluently

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:48.420
you have to translate it in your head first, I was very uncomfortable with the grammar order

00:16:48.910 --> 00:16:55.790
because it is a completely different kind of thinking, which makes grammar the most difficult part for us

00:16:57.530 --> 00:17:04.650
Right, I think all languages have their own forms that we have to get used to

00:17:05.820 --> 00:17:14.420
you need to speak more and listen more

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:21.180
slowly your brain will get used to it, don't overcomplicate it

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:25.470
At first I thought it must be wrong

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:33.480
It's impossible. How can they be in that way, but slowly I get used to it

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:42.860
all languages are like that

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:42.860
Yeah

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:48.870
No matter Japanese, Korean or Chinese

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:53.990
the SEA countries

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:56.210
within their cultures

00:17:56.820 --> 00:18:05.340
China has the longest history and has influenced its neighboring countries

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:14.500
I think its culture is very valuable and of course in the west

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:19.260
we mainly learn western history

00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:22.350
know very little about the East

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:26.920
Now I'm studying Arabic, Turkish and Persian

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:31.290
I began to discover the central Asia has very interesting history that influenced the world

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:41.160
so I think there's a lot of things that we can discover through languages

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:42.600
Very interesting

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:49.950
Oh, that's interesting, and as a Chinese

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:55.680
by mastering the Japanese language, I think I really have a deeper understanding in the

00:18:56.110 --> 00:19:03.430
Japanese culture and their way of thinking

